WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.020
Most of your cells have just one nucleus.

2
00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:04.600
It looks like a rule.

3
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:07.760
A red blood cell in a
mammal has none at all.

4
00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:10.240
It is lost as the cell matures.

5
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:16.080
A skeletal muscle fibre has hundreds, because
it forms when many cells fuse together.

6
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:19.690
So how does a cell's build
match the job it does?

7
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:23.440
In this mission, you'll meet cells
built for very different jobs,

8
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.620
in animals and in plants.

9
00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:30.010
Then you'll decide what a cell's features
can tell you about the work it does.

10
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:34.190
Your mission: find out how a
cell's build matches its job.
